  "producers": "No spawn call site in this binary passes a live scope.  The 14 spawn bodies carrying the increment idiom have 16 direct call sites between them; at every site the last r9 write before the call is `xor %r9d,%r9d`, and no indirect reference (slot call, lea, relocated data pointer) names any of the 14.  The three packet families\u2019 callers are unscoped spawns: the vendored threadpool crate (caller_x4), tokio\u2019s blocking pool (caller_x5), and a std-functions / lazy_mutex spawn (caller_a).  Every packet cell of these families therefore carries a null context, and the ScopeData ledger in the payload drops never fires for them."
